00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.680
Farewell, Rinna

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:07.140
Episode Twelve: 
Confession

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.440
We did it!
We did it!

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.910
Well, Christmas is actually tomorrow, but...

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.530
But the Eve feels more like Christmas.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.170
Hey, hey, don't you all have sweethearts?

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:24.350
You don't?

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.050
You're supposed to spend Christmas Eve with your sweetheart.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.360
Right?
I'll pass.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:31.890
That's no fun.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:33.510
What about you, Dai-chan?

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:33.980
What?

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.620
Err...

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.020
Yeah...

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.180
What about you, Pierre?

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.240
Don't ask me.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.720
Speaking of which, what about you, Kouta?

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.190
Didn't the nurse come and see you recently?

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.530
Whoa!
Really?

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.270
No, that is...

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:59.000
You pulled off an amazing feat against Miss Machida recently, right?

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:00.900
She says she became a fan after that.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:04.340
All right! Kouta's popular!

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.190
That's not true.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:10.560
"Talented hawks hide their talons." They say people like that are cool.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:14.080
At best, we're the talons.

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.700
You mean, "We're red peppers."

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:18.880
You did pulverize Ayaka Machida, after all.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.080
That's true. You treated her just like a kid, too.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.780
Now then, how about we join the decorating team?

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.040
There's no need to worry about her.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:27.700
What?

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:28.740
leave it to me!

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:29.440
I'll leave it to you.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.630
About Ayaka Machida.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.730
But...

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:34.820
This isn't the first time...

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.710
...that she's done something like that.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:43.810
It couldn't be that your injuries were...

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:47.800
Shipon.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:48.290
Yes?

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.270
Get the pumpkin.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.370
R-Right!

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.320
What do you think?

00:03:56.450 --> 00:03:57.780
Oh...?

00:03:57.860 --> 00:03:59.510
What is that, a panda?

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.200
No! It's Rinna!

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.250
At first, I thought it was just an accident.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.720
But as I laid there in the hospital bed, as I thought about that incident...

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:22.360
...I began thinking there was no mistaking she'd done it on purpose.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:26.750
Although I really hated myself for thinking that...

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:30.890
...unfortunately, it looks like I was right.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.520
I'm sorry, Shipon.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:37.940
If I had realized it sooner, then that wouldn't have happened...

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:39.910
That doesn't matter...

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.800
More importantly, you...

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:48.550
I'm all right. It was over two years ago.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.220
I can't cut it.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:00.610
Merry Christmas!

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:05.410
Well, hello, beautiful young miss. Is there something you want?

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.640
Everything is in this sack.

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:12.900
A doll? A dress? Or might you want a ring?

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.290
A hand.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:17.410
A hand?

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:19.010
Um...

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:21.640
You certainly want an unusual thing.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.040
I'm saying that we don't have enough help.

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:28.840
Neither the decorating nor the cooking have been finished yet.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:45.750
They say the mysterious flying objects appeared again.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.410
The ones near the Ultima?

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.430
The Great Mission is over, so now what's the disturbance?

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.640
It's not a disturbance, right?

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:56.020
Then, what?

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:56.650
Who knows?

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.180
The Ultima has it tough.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.810
They say that they've confirmed abnormal responses...

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:04.080
...even from the area where the star went supernova.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:10.560
So everything not okay even though the Great Mission was a success.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:11.950
Okay, I'm done.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:15.190
Good work.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:19.610
Hey, how about the three of us go drinking, since it's been a while.

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:22.530
Sorry, I already have plans. 
What?

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.820
Tonight's Christmas Eve, after all.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.620
But didn't you say you broke up recently?

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.760
We did break up. This is someone new.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.090
I hadn't heard anything!

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.620
I hadn't said anything.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.380
Okay, then, please take care of locking things up.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.500
H-Hey!

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.410
Well then, everyone, have a wonderful evening.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:54.050
I believe expulsion is too heavy a punishment.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:58.080
It's still not definite it will be that.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:00.310
It all depends on the upcoming inquiry...

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.670
...so there's a chance this verdict will be overturned.

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:03.650
Inquiry?

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:07.070
There's a question as to whether she intentionally injured...

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.230
...a preparatory student, Yayoi Fujisawa, two years ago.

00:07:09.870 --> 00:07:11.060
Fujisawa?

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:12.730
I see...

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:25.870
Even though the Great Mission is over, things haven't gotten any easier.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:29.880
How are things there? Are you enjoying Christmas?

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:32.800
We made sure to buy presents for you.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.230
Rinna looks like her mother.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:37.580
It's something so big that it won't fit in a stocking. 

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.830
But the shape of her eyebrows are her father's, right?

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:41.010
That's right, because even though the Great Mission has ended safely... Really?

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:40.410
Aren't they drawn on?

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.660
...we've made you lonely. 

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:43.560
This video is from four hours ago, right?

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:44.540
Five hours.

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.910
The Ultima is far away, isn't it?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.310
It takes five hours just for a phone call.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.040
Yeah.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.260
All right, then, we're going to hang up.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:55.500
Have a merry Christmas.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:58.470
Would you like to reply?

00:07:58.740 --> 00:07:59.370
Of course.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:03.870
Recording. Please start your message after the tone.

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:10.780
Hiya, it's Rinna!

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.410
Classes here are over, and it's winter vacation.

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:15.970
Everyone's going to have a combination Christmas...

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.430
...and farewell party for me after this.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:19.910
We're everyone!

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:21.700
P-Pleased to meet you.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:22.710
Yay!

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:23.930
Hello.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:29.850
All right, then I'm going to go and get the drinks we ordered.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.870
Boys, are you planning on making Milady carry them by herself?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:35.090
Of course not!

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:38.900
It's obvious that I'll carry them, right, Yayoi?

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:41.970
You still haven't finished making the tree decorations.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.820
What?
I'll go.

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:45.180
What? Kouta...

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:47.320
Thank you.

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:48.650
You're welcome.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.500
I'm so jealous...

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.750
And thus, the drinks will be okay.

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:58.080
The cooking's done, so all that's left is the decorating...

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:02.010
Oh, that's right, I have to borrow a star from upperclassman Syoujin.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:02.880
A star?

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.300
That's right, a star.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.090
What, you're sold out?

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.710
I'm sorry, just now...

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.350
...there was a person who bought a whole lot of them.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:22.540
If there's no star at the top, it just won't look right...

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:25.920
If something similar is all right...

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:28.350
Y-You're...

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.620
I have many of them in my room.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.370
I-I see...

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.330
Why does upperclassman Syoujin have stars in his room?

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:39.310
Who knows?

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:41.650
He's a mysterious person, as always.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:44.550
The Big Four is full of weird people.

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:47.140
Upperclassman Najima is strange, too.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.230
I've never heard her speak normally.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.720
Upperclassman Kent seems to be upstanding, though.

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:54.700
They say his hobby is going around deserted houses.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:55.720
What's with that?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.830
Huh? Shipon?

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:02.070
I'll go to upperclassman Syoujin's room.

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.310
Shipon?

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:05.770
Maybe she's in love with upperclassman Syoujin?

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:07.330
It couldn't be.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.070
W-What?

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:13.840
This is...

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:16.810
You can go ahead and color it.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.000
Okay...

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:20.920
Is just one enough?

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:21.910
Oh, yes.

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.010
I see.

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:28.820
U-Um...

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:29.220
Hmm?

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:33.300
Do you know what happened to Ayaka Machida?

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.760
There's nothing to worry about. She was the one at fault.

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.260
Please tell me.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.890
It looks like she hasn't come to school since then...

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:44.110
It couldn't be that she's quit, could it?

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.550
It hasn't been decided yet...

00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:50.010
...but it looks like she'll be expelled.

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:16.330
Christmas is no different, even here in space.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:17.430
That's true.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:21.500
The only disappointing thing is that it can't be a white Christmas.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.050
This year, it'll be a red Christmas.

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:30.960
That's true. But this might just be nice, too.

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:32.350
Um...
Hmm?

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:35.760
Shima-chan didn't seem very happy.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:37.190
What? Well...

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.030
Did something happen?

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:42.240
Kouta, would you give her your support?

00:11:42.840 --> 00:11:44.490
Shipon is...
Fujisawa!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:48.680
Oh, my.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:50.160
Hello.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:57.220
Can I talk to you for a bit?

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:04.440
It's about Ayaka Machida.

00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.240
Welcome back. Where's Milady?

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:11.250
She met an acquaintance on the way back.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:12.770
She'll come back later.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.000
Was it a guy or a girl?!

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.390
A guy. 
This is bad!

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.440
Hey! No slacking!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:22.920
Where's Shima-chan?

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:23.410
Huh?

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.640
Oh, yeah, I wonder what's happened to her.

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:26.590
I haven't seen her.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:27.810
Yeah, really.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:29.490
Did she get lost?

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:30.900
She might be.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:34.600
Recently it took her two hours to come back from the library.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.660
That's very Shipon.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:37.680
That's true.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:40.450
I'm going to look for her.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:49.760
Even though we're called the Big Four...

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.130
...Ayaka is two years younger than us.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:54.200
Even if her grades are the same...

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.810
...I think there are a lot of times where she overextended herself.

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:02.480
Your injuries from two years ago, is it true they were Ayaka's fault?

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:03.810
Straightforward, aren't you?

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.560
It looks like she's going to be expelled.

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:10.610
But they say if this was the first indiscretion...

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:13.060
...there'd be room to take extenuating circumstances into consideration.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:18.830
So her future will be decided based on my testimony.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:26.600
There's no way... I can forgive her, is there?

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:31.340
I don't understand...

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:41.370
I wonder if I did something bad to Miss Machida.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:43.280
Why did she do something like that?

00:13:45.650 --> 00:13:46.850
Otoyama?

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.460
So you were here after all.

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:50.970
What's wrong?

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:53.600
They say that she's... under indefinite suspension...

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:54.670
Miss Machida?

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.940
So it is bothering you.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:01.070
It would bother anyone!

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:04.300
That someone I know would do something like that...

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:07.570
It's scary...

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:09.180
Scary?

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:13.650
I don't know why Miss Machida would do something like that...

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:17.030
And I'm starting to think...

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:20.470
...that maybe other people hate me the way Miss Machida does.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:26.450
Even though it's Christmas, even though it's Rinna's farewell party...

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:28.680
...I can't get into a festive mood.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:32.010
Then let's go. 
What?

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:34.230
Together.

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:48.740
Kent? If you're worried about me, I'm already...

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:56.120
You two!

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:57.570
Hello...

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.590
Your door is insecure.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.280
What do you want?

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.570
Um... I wanted to know...

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:12.370
Why did you...

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:16.480
Why did I try to injure you?

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:20.760
You are meaner than I thought.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:23.300
So you're planning on making me tell you?

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:24.880
That's not what I meant...

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:26.600
Please answer her.

00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:32.730
You'd better answer, right, Ayaka Machida?

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:38.890
You...

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:43.810
You were getting close to me, so I was trying to knock you down.

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:45.190
That's all.

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:49.010
I've been doing that all the way, up until now.

00:15:49.670 --> 00:15:51.260
Farewell, Rinna

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.740
It was the same when I did it to Yayoi.

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:57.220
That wasn't an accident.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:00.320
It was an incident... that I caused.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:02.890
Miss Machida, why?

00:16:03.590 --> 00:16:04.690
I didn't want to lose!

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.730
Not to Yayoi, not to you, not to anyone!

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:14.460
I can't afford to lose... I'm Ayaka Machida, after all.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:20.240
Is it so important to win, to get good grades?

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:22.580
I'm sure you don't understand.

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:29.210
When I lost to you, I realized how petty my pride was.

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.220
That is...

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.480
People like you are what they call true geniuses.

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:36.030
At best, I'm a prodigy...

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:40.020
I buckled down and practiced so much more than other people...

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:41.490
It's unbecoming...

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:43.520
You've heard enough, right?

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:44.620
Let's go.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:49.420
Um, thank you very much.

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:55.570
For... being honest.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:06.770
Kouta and Shipon haven't come back yet, have they?

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:08.560
They're on a date, right?

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:09.360
No way!

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:10.590
Am I wrong?

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:13.420
Could that... be it?

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:14.600
Could it?

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:17.730
No way. Masaru just has it wrong.

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.430
Right, Yayoi...

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:21.220
Yayoi?

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:24.780
Hey, have you seen my Santa outfit?

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:30.390
Merry Christmas.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:43.860
Is that you... Yayoi?

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:00.470
Tell me.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:05.960
Two years ago, back then... you tried to rescue me.

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:22.180
Shima Katase was... she was able to rescue the girl.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:25.390
But I wasn't able to save you.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:31.870
There are things she can do that I can't.

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:34.800
Even though I know she's better than me...

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:38.140
...at the Joust, even during the Great Mission...

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:40.340
There was no merit to it.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:45.000
There was no merit for me to knock you down...

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:57.430
You're the one who attacked me...

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:01.020
But you're also the one who tried to rescue me...

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:04.860
I'm the one who can't forgive you.

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:09.490
But... I'm also the one who thinks she wants to forgive you...

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:15.300
The first time I lost to Miss Machida...

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:16.260
Hmm?

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:19.640
I was really frustrated, so much I cried.

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:23.920
So I can kind of understand how she feels.

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:29.880
I can't forgive what she did, but I can't condemn her...

00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:30.890
I see...

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:32.220
Yeah.

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:36.270
Otoyama, do you ever get frustrated, or think that you want to win?

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:37.220
I do.

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:39.590
You don't seem that way at all.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:43.500
I get told that a lot, that people don't know what I'm thinking.

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:47.310
I'm pretty bad at saying how I feel.

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:49.420
I'm not any good at talking.

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:51.270
Is that something that frustrates you?

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:54.890
It frustrates me that I can't say how I feel.

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:57.640
Even more so when it's a person I like.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:58.190
What?

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:09.030
Because I'm not good at talking...

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:11.920
What?

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.770
Miss Fujisawa has?

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:23.550
Yes.

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.580
She says the incident from two years ago couldn't have been intentional.

00:20:28.110 --> 00:20:32.250
This is from the person who saw the incident from the closest viewpoint.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:35.750
Judges do not exist to punish people.

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:37.890
They exist to forgive people.

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:39.510
Right.

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:42.630
Help me!

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:43.990
Help!

00:20:56.630 --> 00:21:02.180
Glory to God in the highest, and on earth peace...

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.090
...good will towards men.

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:29.540
Infi needs to celebrate, too.

00:21:34.130 --> 00:21:35.230
Merry Christmas.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.050
Merry Christmas.

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
And still I looked up

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next Episode

